--TEST--
A class constant whose value does not have its declared type is `E0401` at the value, where it is declared, whether or not anything reads it
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The first class shows values that fit: `3` in a `float`, `null` in a
// nullable type, and a member of a union.
class Accepted {
    public const float RATE = 3;
    public const ?int NONE = null;
    public const int|string KEY = "id";
    public const array<float> STEPS = [1, 2.5];
}

class Wrong {
    public const uint WIDTH = -1;
    public const int SIZE = "a";
    public const array<int> IDS = [1, "b"];
    public const bool ON = 1;
}

echo Accepted::RATE, " ", Accepted::KEY, " ", Accepted::STEPS[1], "\n";
echo Wrong::SIZE, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: the value of the constant `WIDTH` does not have its declared type `uint`
%A
12 |     public const uint WIDTH = -1;
   |                               ^^ this value is not of type `uint`
%A
error[E0401]: the value of the constant `SIZE` does not have its declared type `int`
%A
13 |     public const int SIZE = "a";
%A
error[E0401]: the value of the constant `IDS` does not have its declared type `array<int>`
%A
14 |     public const array<int> IDS = [1, "b"];
%A
error[E0401]: the value of the constant `ON` does not have its declared type `bool`
%A
15 |     public const bool ON = 1;
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
